1
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:43,970
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:46,890
[Episode 20]

3
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:49,289
[Surgery in Progress]

4
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,479
Dr. Liu.

5
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:50,150
I've read your resume.

6
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:50,410
[Touch-free Faucet]

7
00:01:50,229 --> 00:01:50,789
You're excellent.

8
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:58,880
[Surgical Hand Scrubbing and Antisepsis Procedure]
[Seven-Step Handwashing Technique]

9
00:01:50,789 --> 00:01:53,200
But why do you choose to stay
at Xiaoximen Hospital?

10
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,200
That's personal.

11
00:01:56,789 --> 00:01:59,120
You're more of a character than they said.

12
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,040
I just don't want to talk

13
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,840
about things unrelated to work.

14
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,870
Some small hospitals

15
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:08,000
are kept afloat

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,729
by just one or two good doctors.

17
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,630
These hospitals need doctors

18
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,400
far more than

19
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,960
doctors need them.

20
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,960
You are so young.

21
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,190
You should think about

22
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:20,150
your future.

23
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,750
You need a bigger platform,

24
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:24,430
not one that exploits you.

25
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:31,770
Even the best of us make mistakes.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,660
Even a good horse can stumble.

27
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,240
I don't know your name yet.

28
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,450
Liu Zhengliang.

29
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,930
Liu Zhengliang.

30
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:49,079
Don't you hold a grudge against me?

31
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:50,240
They say

32
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:52,280
I pulled a knife on you that day.

33
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,079
I'll have to pull a knife

34
00:02:53,079 --> 00:02:54,430
on you in a bit.

35
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,710
Before, I never thought

36
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,120
being a doctor or a police

37
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,000
was so great.

38
00:03:07,470 --> 00:03:08,150
Aren't they all just jobs

39
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:09,800
that put food on the table?

40
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,690
That is, until I met you.

41
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,120
If I were you,

42
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,590
I couldn't do what you do.

43
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,470
Really.

44
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,030
That day,

45
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:24,360
you said in the hall

46
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:26,240
that you were a good doctor.

47
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,360
Now I believe that.

48
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:30,680
Thank you.

49
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,450
Thank me after the surgery is successful.

50
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:38,520
Anesthesia.

51
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,360
Wait a minute.

52
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:48,310
If I don't survive,

53
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:52,030
please tell Su Jing

54
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:55,280
to keep appealing.

55
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:57,280
Don't let it affect

56
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,010
our child's chances
of getting a government job.

57
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,710
Take a deep breath.

58
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:06,520
With this fighting spirit,

59
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,380
he'll pull through this surgery.

60
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:10,550
He's got the will to live.

61
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,280
Right temporal craniotomy completed.

62
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:17,920
The surgical field is well exposed.

63
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,070
Now we have to

64
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:21,130
determine the boundary of the tumor.

65
00:04:21,339 --> 00:04:22,720
The boundary between
the tumor and the cortex

66
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,830
is hard to determine.

67
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:24,670
So I need to

68
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:25,800
open the cortex

69
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:28,070
and assess the color and texture

70
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,070
before I can determine
the tumor's boundaries.

71
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,730
That's excellent technique.

72
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,950
His technique is second to none.

73
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:34,800
Yes.

74
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:37,390
You two, watch carefully

75
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:38,480
and learn from this.

76
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,280
You don't get opportunities like this
very often.

77
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:43,830
The tumor in the temporal lobe

78
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:45,720
doesn't look too difficult to remove.

79
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,040
Can you operate?

80
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,640
No problem. I'll start then.

81
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,270
The brain tissue is swelling

82
00:04:58,270 --> 00:04:59,159
too fast.

83
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,070
Severe cerebral swelling.

84
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:02,950
This is one of the most dangerous

85
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,730
complications of craniotomy.

86
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:07,410
Can you determine
the cause of the swelling?

87
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:09,560
Is it internal bleeding in the tumor,

88
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,950
or something else?

89
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:13,120
Could the old injury have started

90
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,720
bleeding again?

91
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,390
Impossible.

92
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:16,190
There's no problem with the trauma.

93
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,360
It looks like
the draining vein was cut first,

94
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,680
before the main feeding artery

95
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:20,600
was blocked.

96
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,070
Here.

97
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,160
Take a piece of wet gauze

98
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,160
and press it gently for me.

99
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,360
Keep the brain protected for now.

100
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,510
I'll find the main feeding artery

101
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:26,190
and block it.

102
00:05:26,190 --> 00:05:27,650
Blood pressure 75 over 38.

103
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:29,160
Give vasopressors immediately,

104
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,510
and another bottle of colloid fluid.

105
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:33,510
Contact the blood bank
and prepare for a transfusion!

106
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,800
Found it.

107
00:05:35,190 --> 00:05:37,190
I've found the main feeding artery.

108
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,270
Okay.

109
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,390
The swelling is finally going down.

110
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:45,250
His blood pressure is stable too.

111
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:48,920
Okay.

112
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:51,770
Then let's continue removing the tumor.

113
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:57,310
[Do not touch the louvers]

114
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:01,960
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

115
00:06:04,310 --> 00:06:10,820
[Quiet]

116
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:06,310
Du Fang's family.

117
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,190
The surgery went very well.

118
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:09,040
Don't worry.

119
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,870
Thank you.

120
00:06:17,770 --> 00:06:23,210
[Kindly close the door behind you]

121
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:33,830
I watched

122
00:06:34,159 --> 00:06:35,870
the surgery from beginning to end.

123
00:06:35,870 --> 00:06:37,470
Your skills are really good.

124
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:39,480
Your talent is being wasted

125
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,870
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

126
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:43,750
Chief Physician Qin has her eye on you.

127
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:45,150
She asked me to talk to you

128
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,360
and see if you're willing to join us.

129
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:49,390
Your current rank will carry over,
of course,

130
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:50,750
and your income will double.

131
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,010
That's very generous.

132
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,270
Qin

133
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:54,630
is about to retire.

134
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,720
Then you can handle the clinical side,

135
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,000
and I'll handle the research.

136
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,240
With our partnership,

137
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,390
give us 3 years,

138
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,870
and we'll be one of the top 3

139
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:03,950
neurosurgery departments in the province.

140
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:05,000
You'd never reach

141
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:05,920
an achievement like this

142
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,250
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

143
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:08,870
What do you think?

144
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:12,040
This offer is good.

145
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:14,870
So you agree?

146
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,360
I have a question.

147
00:07:22,190 --> 00:07:22,950
Go ahead.

148
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:24,950
If I go there,

149
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:27,240
which one of us will be the boss?

150
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,680
I'll be the boss, of course.

151
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,480
Then I won't go.

152
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,630
After all, I like

153
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:35,240
giving orders.

154
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,920
Look, I just criticized you a bit.

155
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,630
Why do you still hold a grudge?

156
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,240
Okay.

157
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,190
I'll treat you to a drink tonight, okay?

158
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:43,920
How about you treat me instead?

159
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,720
President Long.

160
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,240
You're poaching my people on my turf.

161
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,900
Isn't that crossing the line?

162
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:53,710
Chief Physician Liu,
someone is looking for you outside.

163
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:57,720
President.

164
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,500
Well, President Long,

165
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,240
this isn't poaching.

166
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:09,780
At most, we were just talking it over.

167
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,920
Besides, I can

168
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:14,380
wait for Chief Physician Liu
to lose his job.

169
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,390
I'll treat you
to a drink another day,

170
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:17,870
okay?

171
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:21,630
If there's nothing else, President Long,

172
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,190
I-I'll take my leave.

173
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,650
Why are you here?

174
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:46,600
I need to talk to you about something.

175
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,600
Come with me.

176
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:50,150
Let's have a talk.

177
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,750
Okay.

178
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,120
Then wait for me a sec.

179
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,080
I just finished a surgery

180
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:54,790
and need to take a shower.

181
00:08:54,790 --> 00:08:55,840
No need.

182
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:59,040
Let's go take a shower together.

183
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,750
Come down.

184
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:20,380
[Shower]

185
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:18,550
I haven't

186
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:19,440
set foot in

187
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,440
a public bathhouse in over 20 years.

188
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:23,810
I'm not used to this anymore,
so I'll pass.

189
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:26,670
So you don't want

190
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:28,600
to be naked in front of me?

191
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:30,480
Fine.

192
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:34,150
Clothes can cover your body,

193
00:09:36,390 --> 00:09:38,030
but you've got to open up

194
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,750
to me here.

195
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,870
The heart is responsible
for pumping blood.

196
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:46,630
If I open it up

197
00:09:46,630 --> 00:09:47,360
to you,

198
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,480
I'll die.

199
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,630
Playing dumb with me, huh?

200
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,130
Believe it or not, I'll beat you up.

201
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:03,200
Come on, come down.

202
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,650
Just a foot soak is fine.

203
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:07,720
Then we can

204
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,870
at least say

205
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:13,120
we've soaked our feet

206
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,750
in the same pool.

207
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:18,530
I might like you a little more.

208
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,770
What exactly do you want to tell me?

209
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:41,360
Scrub my back later.

210
00:10:42,270 --> 00:10:43,930
I've said what I needed to say.

211
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,480
Figure it out yourself.

212
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,660
Learn from Ai Chen.

213
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:57,270
Try opening your heart.

214
00:11:12,510 --> 00:11:13,440
Why are you here?

215
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,200
You came back just in time.

216
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,440
It's almost heated up.

217
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:17,870
What is it?

218
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:19,550
My mom stewed two pork joints today.

219
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:21,550
She asked me to bring one for you two.

220
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:23,390
She also made dumplings. Look.

221
00:11:23,390 --> 00:11:24,120
It smells so good.

222
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,840
Of course.

223
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,270
Do you know

224
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:28,930
what Zhengguang just told me?

225
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:30,550
What did he say?

226
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,260
He said he's going to Beijing.

227
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,390
Careful, it's hot.

228
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:34,030
It's fine.

229
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:36,670
He's leaving tomorrow.

230
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:37,670
He already bought the ticket.

231
00:11:37,670 --> 00:11:38,390
Tomorrow?

232
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:39,240
Exactly.

233
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,550
That's too sudden.

234
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:41,480
Go ask him.

235
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:42,960
Ask him.

236
00:11:48,270 --> 00:11:49,200
Liu Zhengguang.

237
00:11:50,150 --> 00:11:52,030
You're going to Beijing tomorrow?

238
00:11:52,030 --> 00:11:53,890
Why didn't you discuss it with me?

239
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,750
It's my life. I'll make my own decisions.

240
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,080
I don't need to discuss it with you.

241
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,740
What are you even deciding on?

242
00:11:59,120 --> 00:11:59,720
Didn't you just get a job

243
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,850
at a massage parlor?

244
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,510
The salary is too low. There's no future.

245
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:05,510
I don't want to do it anymore.

246
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,390
I've only been back for a few days,

247
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:08,270
and now you're leaving already?

248
00:12:08,270 --> 00:12:08,870
Didn't we agree

249
00:12:08,870 --> 00:12:10,200
to spend some time together?

250
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,400
That's what you said.

251
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,840
Didn't you also say

252
00:12:13,030 --> 00:12:15,090
you'd support me no matter what I did?

253
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:17,840
Yes.

254
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:19,000
I did say that.

255
00:12:19,390 --> 00:12:22,000
He has said a lot of things.

256
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,750
You don't listen to everything he says.

257
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:26,360
You said you needed some time
to figure things out,

258
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,030
right?

259
00:12:27,270 --> 00:12:28,510
It's only been two months.

260
00:12:28,510 --> 00:12:29,510
And you're ready?

261
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:31,120
No.

262
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,290
But I've figured it out.

263
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:34,440
If I never take the first step,

264
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,600
I'll never be ready.

265
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,120
Don't act like

266
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,270
you're so brave.

267
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:39,000
Have you thought this through?

268
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,480
I have no degree,

269
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:41,510
no background,

270
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,510
and no money.

271
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:44,270
I've only got two things going for me:

272
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,270
courage

273
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,550
and youth.

274
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:47,840
But

275
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,150
both of those

276
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:51,320
will fade with time,

277
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,320
until I truly have nothing.

278
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:54,960
Come on.

279
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,080
Save that crap.

280
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,240
Y-Your relatives,

281
00:12:58,270 --> 00:13:00,270
friends, and home are all here.

282
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,480
And you're going to Beijing?

283
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,840
That's what it means to have nothing.

284
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,600
Get it?

285
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,240
Right?

286
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,360
Speak.

287
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:13,550
Have you really thought it through?

288
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,870
I have.

289
00:13:15,270 --> 00:13:16,230
I didn't I tell you

290
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:17,030
in advance

291
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:17,750
because I knew

292
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:18,240
you'd

293
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,640
react exactly like this.

294
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:33,910
I'll sell this house,

295
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:37,330
and you can keep all the money.

296
00:13:39,910 --> 00:13:40,790
Plus the cash

297
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:42,120
Mom left behind.

298
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,440
You can use it

299
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,900
to get started in Beijing.

300
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:46,550
Do you remember

301
00:13:46,550 --> 00:13:47,550
what I told you

302
00:13:47,550 --> 00:13:48,810
when I first came back?

303
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:50,480
I said,

304
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,510
I'm your big brother,

305
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,080
so it's

306
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,030
my job

307
00:13:55,030 --> 00:13:56,030
to look after you.

308
00:13:56,510 --> 00:13:57,270
Since I said it,

309
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:58,390
I have to do it.

310
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,150
Liu Zhengliang.

311
00:13:59,150 --> 00:13:59,910
And

312
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,820
I agree with what you said.

313
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:03,360
Indeed.

314
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:07,680
If you don't take a shot now,
you'll be too old before you know it.

315
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:10,960
So just go.

316
00:14:11,630 --> 00:14:12,870
What's the big deal?

317
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:14,080
If you can't make it, just come back.

318
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,010
Liu Zhengliang.

319
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,230
Easy.

320
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:17,980
How about this?

321
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:20,090
Tomorrow morning,

322
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,840
I'll go to the real estate agency.

323
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,570
Zhengliang.

324
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:23,890
I know you're touched.

325
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,750
I also think I'm pretty great.

326
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:28,550
No, Zhengliang.

327
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:29,880
Stop talking nonsense.

328
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,200
Hurry up and pack.

329
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,110
There's no time. Let's go.

330
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:33,040
Liu Zhengliang.

331
00:14:33,630 --> 00:14:34,790
I mean,

332
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:35,390
you don't have to

333
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:36,870
sell the house over this.

334
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:43,960
You don't need to walk me out.

335
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,120
I didn't plan to.

336
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,670
Just wanted to tell you something.

337
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:48,960
Your dad came to see me
a couple of days ago.

338
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,750
For what?

339
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,910
He dragged me off to the bathhouse

340
00:14:52,910 --> 00:14:55,570
and said something
that didn't make much sense.

341
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:56,360
Whatever he said to you,

342
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,670
don't take it to heart.

343
00:14:58,790 --> 00:14:59,960
I'll ask him later.

344
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,550
No need. Don't ask him.

345
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:03,350
I just wanted to let you know.

346
00:15:04,910 --> 00:15:05,720
What's wrong?

347
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:06,920
You're still angry?

348
00:15:07,550 --> 00:15:10,350
There's nothing wrong with
what Zhengguang said.

349
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,840
I'm not angry at Zhengguang.

350
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,360
Then who are you angry at?

351
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,390
Me?

352
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:18,750
I'm not angry at anyone.

353
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,750
I'm just mad at the Northeast.

354
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:28,630
Were we born in the Northeast

355
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:30,200
just to leave it behind?

356
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,030
I've seen many people leave,

357
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:36,150
and I've helped many return
to their roots.

358
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:38,000
But I just don't get it.

359
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,240
Are they all afraid of the cold,

360
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,840
or are they allergic to snow?

361
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:43,550
Winters in the Northeast are cold,

362
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:45,550
but the people are warm.

363
00:15:48,270 --> 00:15:50,730
Is the outside world
really that wonderful?

364
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,300
Will leaving the Northeast
make them happy?

365
00:15:56,870 --> 00:15:58,510
Don't they miss home?

366
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:04,750
I've been out there,

367
00:16:05,510 --> 00:16:07,320
but what's good or bad
depends on how you look at it.

368
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,320
Everyone has different standards.

369
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:11,790
Whether the outside world is good or not—

370
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:12,920
I can't answer that.

371
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:14,750
But I can answer

372
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:15,880
your last question.

373
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,320
They miss home.

374
00:16:20,750 --> 00:16:22,550
From the day they leave home

375
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:24,750
to the day

376
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:25,950
they finally return.

377
00:16:32,390 --> 00:16:33,920
Your luggage is all packed?

378
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,790
You...

379
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:36,910
You've got a lot going for you.

380
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:38,150
You're just too impulsive.

381
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:40,000
You just do whatever pops into your head

382
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,270
and now take off on a whim.

383
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:42,960
We just started to get along.

384
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,330
Wait till I get back.

385
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,390
By the time I come back,

386
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:47,360
I'll probably be rolling in money.

387
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,290
By then, I'll...

388
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,790
Slow down.

389
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,390
And you said I'm impulsive.

390
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,600
When I come back,

391
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,480
I'll have this shop of yours

392
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,120
renovated.

393
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,030
And I'll invest in you.

394
00:16:58,030 --> 00:16:59,790
Come on.

395
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,320
Just make sure you don't starve out there.

396
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:04,200
And you want to invest in me?

397
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:08,109
Take this.

398
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:10,440
I can't take this.

399
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,240
You don't want your pay?

400
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:14,109
I only worked for six days this month.

401
00:17:14,109 --> 00:17:15,200
So what if it's six days?

402
00:17:14,569 --> 00:17:17,750
[Gong's Blind Massage]

403
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:16,160
Take it.

404
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:17,829
The extra

405
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,069
is to help you out.

406
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,680
You need money when you're traveling.

407
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:22,510
Take it, kid.

408
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:24,960
Thank you.

409
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:25,960
Don't mention it.

410
00:17:27,310 --> 00:17:28,109
Zhengguang.

411
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,880
Sweetie, careful.

412
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,590
Why are you here?

413
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,550
You guys are making

414
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:36,550
such a fuss over me leaving.

415
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:37,880
I'm not used to all this.

416
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,830
Good luck. Have a safe trip.

417
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:44,720
Got it.

418
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,240
I... I'm leaving.

419
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:52,790
I'll walk you out.

420
00:18:09,510 --> 00:18:11,750
Hope you find someone special soon.

421
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,780
Consider this my contribution
to your future wedding.

422
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:17,000
Take care.

423
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,160
Zhengguang.

424
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,200
If you can't make it out there,

425
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,240
just come back.

426
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:22,240
Okay.

427
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:34,920
Do you have to go?

428
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,440
I have to.

429
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,200
Only by leaving can I make big money.

430
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,590
You never used to be
so obsessed

431
00:18:40,590 --> 00:18:41,590
with money.

432
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,330
Didn't you say that was in the past?

433
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,160
People change.

434
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,720
Are you leaving because of Gong Xue?

435
00:18:53,310 --> 00:18:54,240
What do you mean?

436
00:18:57,350 --> 00:19:00,150
You want to make money
to pay for her eye treatment.

437
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:05,620
[Parking lot]

438
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:04,000
I make money for myself first.

439
00:19:04,070 --> 00:19:05,000
Enjoying life

440
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,160
is what matters most.

441
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:08,220
It has nothing to do with anyone else.

442
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:14,040
[Parking lot]

443
00:19:16,070 --> 00:19:18,030
So you're leaving because of me?

444
00:19:20,310 --> 00:19:21,110
Exactly.

445
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:22,920
Now you're talking.

446
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,030
Look, here's the thing.

447
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,290
We're buddies, right?

448
00:19:26,070 --> 00:19:27,480
I'll go to Beijing
and see what I can make of it.

449
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,680
Once I make it big,

450
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:31,120
I'll come back
and help you make money too.

451
00:19:31,790 --> 00:19:32,880
Zhengguang, I...

452
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:33,590
Okay, okay.

453
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,730
Come on, enough of that.

454
00:19:35,790 --> 00:19:36,550
You're a grown man.

455
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:37,680
Don't get all mushy.

456
00:19:39,350 --> 00:19:41,200
My friend at the crematorium

457
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,160
told me

458
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,330
that they're hiring a night watchman.

459
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,830
The job also involves
helping carry bodies.

460
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:47,590
The pay is good.

461
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:49,160
Aren't you looking for a job?

462
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,070
If you're not afraid,
why not give it a try?

463
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:51,930
The pay is good.

464
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,880
I'm not afraid.

465
00:19:56,030 --> 00:19:57,680
Let's both do our best.

466
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,570
Let's make it big

467
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:00,680
and give the people

468
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:02,010
around us a better life.

469
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,030
I'm leaving.

470
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,400
Zhengguang.

471
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:13,830
Didn't you say you had surgery today?

472
00:20:13,830 --> 00:20:15,070
Aren't you leaving?

473
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,170
I rushed over as fast as I could.

474
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:17,830
Let's go.

475
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:19,400
There's time to see you in.

476
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,070
Did you bring your ID?

477
00:20:21,070 --> 00:20:22,400
I brought it. I had to.

478
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,030
If I hadn't brought it,

479
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:24,240
I'd have just drawn a fake one

480
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,070
and snuck in.

481
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:27,480
I'm leaving. Go back.

482
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,280
Take care of yourself out there.

483
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:39,610
[Bus Terminal]

484
00:20:39,010 --> 00:20:42,160
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

485
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:45,860
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

486
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,580
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

487
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:47,920
Where's Zhengguang?

488
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:48,790
Over there.

489
00:20:48,990 --> 00:20:51,340
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

490
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:50,880
Didn't you say you weren't coming?

491
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,200
You also said you weren't coming.

492
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,000
Zhengguang.

493
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:56,850
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

494
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,440
Zhengguang!

495
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:55,680
Here.

496
00:20:55,750 --> 00:20:56,480
That ID from before

497
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,270
is with me.

498
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:59,030
Pocket it. It might be useful.

499
00:20:57,330 --> 00:21:00,450
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

500
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,240
I know.

501
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,270
Chen, you keep it.

502
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:03,300
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

503
00:21:01,590 --> 00:21:02,270
I will never

504
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:03,240
lose my ID again.

505
00:21:03,390 --> 00:21:03,870
[Phone Charging Station]

506
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:06,010
♪ How like life it is ♪

507
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:08,030
[Phone Charging Station]

508
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,480
Hello?

509
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:11,530
♪ One who was stranded on the road ♪

510
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:10,640
Speak slowly. I can't hear you clearly.

511
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:12,550
What's wrong?

512
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:15,070
♪ Heels buried under unseen snow ♪

513
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,030
Bye-bye!

514
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,800
♪ Don't panic—the journey is long ♪

515
00:21:18,170 --> 00:21:20,690
♪ Long enough to hold your pause ♪

516
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:25,950
♪ The wind in the city ♪

517
00:21:26,330 --> 00:21:29,080
♪ Blows through dreams
that flicker between light and dark ♪

518
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:32,600
♪ Blows through one soul's radiance ♪

519
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:36,810
♪ And all its weathered scars ♪

520
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:40,480
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

521
00:21:40,790 --> 00:21:43,590
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

522
00:21:44,710 --> 00:21:47,270
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

523
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:54,720
♪ Toward the crossroads
brimming with sunlight ♪

524
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:55,680
[Kindly close the door behind you]

525
00:21:58,270 --> 00:21:59,530
What's the situation?

526
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:01,200
The heart failure is too severe.

527
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:01,880
In the ICU,

528
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,030
he might last 7 or 8 days.

529
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,830
But if he leaves,
he won't last half a day.

530
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:06,760
How could this happen so suddenly?

531
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,830
Chief Physician Qin has checked on him.

532
00:22:08,830 --> 00:22:09,680
It's likely that the patient

533
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:10,880
already had underlying

534
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:12,310
cardiovascular disease.

535
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:14,840
After the surgery,
his body was under stress.

536
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:15,790
Fluctuations in blood pressure

537
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:17,270
or abnormal blood clotting

538
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:24,690
[Equipment Room]

539
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:19,310
may have triggered
a massive myocardial infarction.

540
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:21,000
No one could have done anything.

541
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:21,720
Alright,

542
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,180
it's not our fault either.

543
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,830
Why are you even
bringing up fault right now?

544
00:22:24,830 --> 00:22:26,360
Can you not be so emotional?

545
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:27,860
It's just fate.

546
00:22:28,550 --> 00:22:29,350
We are doctors,

547
00:22:29,350 --> 00:22:30,440
not the Almighty.

548
00:22:29,610 --> 00:22:33,180
[Equipment Room]

549
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:33,030
He's not even 30.

550
00:22:33,750 --> 00:22:35,810
The surgery was clearly successful.

551
00:22:37,750 --> 00:22:38,480
You should

552
00:22:38,790 --> 00:22:39,440
think about

553
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:40,830
how to tell his family.

554
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,040
Yesterday he said

555
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:46,480
he wanted to eat
Eight-Treasure Pork Trotters.

556
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:48,010
He asked me to buy it for him.

557
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,440
I figured that stuff

558
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:51,550
was too greasy,

559
00:22:51,830 --> 00:22:53,230
so I didn't get it for him.

560
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:57,280
I said he could have it
after he was discharged.

561
00:22:59,110 --> 00:23:01,110
How could he be doing so badly today?

562
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,270
He even apologized to me.

563
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,440
He said he didn't know
why he got sick before,

564
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,100
and his temper got really bad.

565
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:15,000
But after the surgery,

566
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,270
he felt different.

567
00:23:17,590 --> 00:23:18,920
Maybe he was cured.

568
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,440
Doctor.

569
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:27,770
Wasn't he getting better?

570
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:33,750
I'm sorry.

571
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,840
We really tried our best.

572
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:37,070
How much does the ICU cost

573
00:23:37,070 --> 00:23:38,350
per day?

574
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:41,550
Even at Xiaoximen Hospital,

575
00:23:41,550 --> 00:23:43,210
it's at least 5,000 to 10,000.

576
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,440
Even in the ICU,

577
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,900
he won't last much longer.

578
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:50,160
And besides, this expense

579
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,880
isn't covered by our agreement.

580
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,590
Our team

581
00:23:52,590 --> 00:23:53,920
can't afford this.

582
00:23:57,030 --> 00:23:58,510
Can we try again?

583
00:23:58,830 --> 00:24:00,230
Think of something else?

584
00:24:14,380 --> 00:24:17,070
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

585
00:24:18,270 --> 00:24:19,070
Okay.

586
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,440
I know.

587
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,310
I'll go borrow money.

588
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:29,610
Can you keep him going a little longer?

589
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:33,680
Ms. Su,

590
00:24:35,270 --> 00:24:36,030
we completely understand

591
00:24:36,030 --> 00:24:37,720
how you feel.

592
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,860
But we need to make this clear.

593
00:24:40,030 --> 00:24:41,360
This isn't about money.

594
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:42,640
The patient already has

595
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:43,310
a consciousness disorder.

596
00:24:43,310 --> 00:24:44,790
He might never pull through.

597
00:24:44,790 --> 00:24:45,920
You don't need to...

598
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:48,160
Alright, say no more!

599
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:52,270
I understand everything.

600
00:24:56,310 --> 00:24:57,030
Okay.

601
00:24:58,110 --> 00:24:59,680
Let me say one last thing.

602
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,100
You're raising a child alone.

603
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,270
You can't ruin

604
00:25:05,270 --> 00:25:06,470
your future for this.

605
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:11,440
Go borrow the money.

606
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,260
I'll keep an eye on him.

607
00:25:14,830 --> 00:25:16,070
If he regains consciousness,

608
00:25:16,070 --> 00:25:17,730
I'll notify you immediately.

609
00:25:21,070 --> 00:25:22,720
Thank you, Dr. Liu.

610
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:25,170
I'll go borrow money right now.

611
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:27,310
I'll be right back.

612
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:31,750
Are you people at Xiaoximen Hospital

613
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:33,210
that desperate for money?

614
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:33,550
Well.

615
00:25:33,550 --> 00:25:35,350
Don't you know her situation?

616
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:37,720
You'd stoop to making money off this, too?

617
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,320
The decision is hers to make.

618
00:25:42,020 --> 00:25:47,300
[Quiet] [Non-Smoking Ward]

619
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:57,410
I'll take over.

620
00:25:57,750 --> 00:25:59,750
Someone is looking for you outside.

621
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:05,200
Aren't the patients in the ICU

622
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:07,480
supposed to be under their care?

623
00:26:08,270 --> 00:26:10,600
Why are you the one
watching him every day?

624
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:13,550
Isn't there a rumor
that the hospital is shutting down?

625
00:26:13,550 --> 00:26:15,610
Many people have resigned recently.

626
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:17,160
Besides,

627
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:18,360
Du Fang is different.

628
00:26:20,830 --> 00:26:23,360
Is Xiaoximen Hospital
really going to close?

629
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:26,590
Not necessarily.

630
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:27,480
Right?

631
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,160
I think so too.

632
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:30,720
A man like President Long

633
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:32,510
is so calculating.

634
00:26:33,310 --> 00:26:34,110
Wouldn't he leave himself

635
00:26:34,110 --> 00:26:35,370
a way out or something?

636
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:38,590
Why don't you go and sound him out?

637
00:26:38,590 --> 00:26:39,790
It won't do any good.

638
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:40,960
I can't change anything.

639
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:41,690
That's true.

640
00:26:41,790 --> 00:26:44,000
There's Sichuan pepper
on that shrimp ball.

641
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,070
Pick it out.

642
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:52,790
Is it good?

643
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:56,510
Not bad.

644
00:26:57,110 --> 00:26:57,960
When it comes to cooking,

645
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,680
I'm pretty confident.

646
00:27:00,510 --> 00:27:02,570
Otherwise, how could I have grown up?

647
00:27:05,550 --> 00:27:06,880
Do you know
why the characters for "grow up"

648
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,640
don't have radicals?

649
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,740
You don't know, do you?

650
00:27:12,350 --> 00:27:14,030
Because you have to rely on yourself.

651
00:27:14,030 --> 00:27:16,490
You have to rely on yourself
for everything.

652
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,640
I almost forgot.

653
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:20,590
When we were kids,

654
00:27:20,590 --> 00:27:22,550
neither of us had our parents around.

655
00:27:22,550 --> 00:27:24,210
So we had to rely on ourselves.

656
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,030
We had to be self-reliant since childhood,

657
00:27:26,030 --> 00:27:26,680
persevere,

658
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:28,480
and one day we'll
accumulate enough strength

659
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:29,480
to make everyone

660
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:30,810
look at us with new eyes.

661
00:27:36,790 --> 00:27:37,720
Listening to the broadcast wasn't in vain.

662
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:38,440
I can tell.

663
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:39,440
I'm so eloquent.

664
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:41,570
Call Su Jing quickly. Du Fang is awake.

665
00:28:04,510 --> 00:28:05,240
Hurry.

666
00:28:05,310 --> 00:28:06,710
You don't have much time.

667
00:28:08,510 --> 00:28:09,240
Let's go.

668
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,280
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

669
00:28:09,660 --> 00:28:10,570
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

670
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,000
Du Fang.

671
00:28:17,550 --> 00:28:18,750
Du Fang, look.

672
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:20,520
I brought our daughter here.

673
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,160
Du Fang.

674
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:26,350
Look.

675
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:50,640
[Standardize Medical Practices
and Ensure Patient Safety]

676
00:28:54,610 --> 00:29:00,740
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

677
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:10,590
Du Fang, what do you want to do?

678
00:29:19,350 --> 00:29:19,880
Come on.

679
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:21,680
Talk to your dad.

680
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:25,310
Dad, I miss you.

681
00:29:30,830 --> 00:29:32,150
Dad misses you too.

682
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,550
Quick, call Dad.

683
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,240
Dad.

684
00:29:55,030 --> 00:29:55,750
Du Fang.

685
00:29:56,590 --> 00:29:57,310
Du Fang.

686
00:29:58,590 --> 00:29:59,480
Du Fang!

687
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:01,200
Open your eyes and look!

688
00:30:01,830 --> 00:30:03,880
I brought our daughter to see you!

689
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:06,590
Du Fang!

690
00:30:06,520 --> 00:30:08,940
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

691
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:08,960
Open your eyes and look!

692
00:30:09,480 --> 00:30:11,750
I brought our child to see you!

693
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:15,480
Du Fang!

694
00:30:16,270 --> 00:30:18,110
Open your eyes.

695
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,920
The police have reopened the investigation

696
00:30:25,020 --> 00:30:28,730
[Welcome to Fangyuan Hotel]

697
00:30:26,590 --> 00:30:28,720
and will give Du Fang a fair result.

698
00:30:28,810 --> 00:30:29,440
[Open]

699
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:31,400
The child will be able to
hold her head high in the future.

700
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:36,680
[Welcome to Fangyuan Hotel]

701
00:30:32,070 --> 00:30:32,880
This

702
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:34,550
was collected by the doctors for you.

703
00:30:34,550 --> 00:30:35,720
This is from the police station.

704
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,270
Everyone there chipped in for you.

705
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:37,830
Don't worry.

706
00:30:37,830 --> 00:30:39,350
Everyone did it voluntarily.

707
00:30:39,350 --> 00:30:40,160
Take it.

708
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,440
How can I accept this?

709
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:43,780
You have to take it.

710
00:30:44,270 --> 00:30:45,510
It's their way of showing they care,

711
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:46,270
you know?

712
00:30:48,750 --> 00:30:50,160
Okay, thank you.

713
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:50,960
Keep it.

714
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:52,400
The day before yesterday,

715
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:53,880
we did the math.

716
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:55,790
All the funeral expenses,

717
00:30:55,790 --> 00:30:57,200
plus the restaurant bill,

718
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:58,550
came to 4,580 altogether,

719
00:30:58,550 --> 00:30:58,960
right?

720
00:30:58,960 --> 00:30:59,640
Right.

721
00:30:59,790 --> 00:31:00,750
Dr. Liu

722
00:31:00,750 --> 00:31:02,550
told me about your situation.

723
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:03,790
Just pay me the cost price.

724
00:31:03,790 --> 00:31:04,830
3,300 is fine.

725
00:31:06,510 --> 00:31:07,310
No.

726
00:31:07,310 --> 00:31:08,510
Just make it 4,580.

727
00:31:09,750 --> 00:31:11,410
Come on, why would you do that?

728
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,920
You've helped too much.

729
00:31:14,030 --> 00:31:15,310
I feel bad about it.

730
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:17,750
I want peace of mind.

731
00:31:19,070 --> 00:31:20,510
As a doctor,

732
00:31:22,310 --> 00:31:24,070
attending a patient's funeral

733
00:31:25,270 --> 00:31:27,200
really makes me feel bad.

734
00:31:30,750 --> 00:31:32,350
He doesn't have any relatives or friends.

735
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:33,680
If we didn't come,

736
00:31:34,070 --> 00:31:35,670
hardly anyone would be here.

737
00:31:37,550 --> 00:31:38,610
I gave it all to her.

738
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:50,010
Thank you all so much for coming today,

739
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:52,480
especially you, Dr. Liu.

740
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,670
Everyone told me

741
00:31:56,790 --> 00:31:57,680
not to put my Du Fang

742
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:58,720
in the ICU.

743
00:31:59,270 --> 00:32:01,130
It would've been a waste of money.

744
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:03,160
I know.

745
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:04,790
They all meant well.

746
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,200
But I just couldn't bring myself

747
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,350
to let it go.

748
00:32:12,790 --> 00:32:14,000
You understood me.

749
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:16,980
You stayed by his side
for me for two days.

750
00:32:18,510 --> 00:32:21,270
Even if he

751
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:23,160
only woke up for a few minutes,

752
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:25,510
at least my daughter and I

753
00:32:25,510 --> 00:32:27,510
got to talk to him for a little while.

754
00:32:27,830 --> 00:32:28,750
Now I know

755
00:32:30,510 --> 00:32:32,240
he won't be making that journey

756
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:34,000
all alone.

757
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:39,010
And I no longer have to worry about him.

758
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:42,720
From now on,

759
00:32:43,350 --> 00:32:45,240
I'll raise my child

760
00:32:46,070 --> 00:32:47,530
and make a good life for us.

761
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:51,880
Thank you, everyone.

762
00:33:06,670 --> 00:33:10,420
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

763
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:14,150
[Hospital Admission Registration]
[Accessible Route]

764
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:18,070
[Emergency]

765
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:38,740
There really aren't many patients, huh?

766
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:42,720
That's true.

767
00:33:43,350 --> 00:33:44,550
I heard people outside spreading rumors,

768
00:33:44,550 --> 00:33:45,920
saying Xiaoximen Hospital
is going to close.

769
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:47,310
Who would come here to see a doctor?

770
00:33:45,970 --> 00:33:49,600
[Stroke Center; Green Channel]

771
00:33:47,830 --> 00:33:49,310
If something goes wrong,

772
00:33:50,110 --> 00:33:52,240
they wouldn't even know who to turn to.

773
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:56,310
I just came from the office.

774
00:33:56,310 --> 00:33:58,710
Where's Mingming? Does she have a surgery?

775
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:01,070
Listen to the question you're asking.

776
00:34:01,070 --> 00:34:02,530
You just said it yourself.

777
00:34:03,030 --> 00:34:04,960
Our hospital is about to shut down.

778
00:34:05,350 --> 00:34:06,310
There are no patients.

779
00:34:06,310 --> 00:34:08,170
How could there be any surgeries?

780
00:34:08,550 --> 00:34:09,550
Mingming went to the provincial capital

781
00:34:09,550 --> 00:34:11,679
on a business trip with the president.

782
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:14,190
What kind of business trip are they on?

783
00:34:14,190 --> 00:34:15,280
Who knows?

784
00:34:15,280 --> 00:34:16,810
Call and ask them yourself.

785
00:34:17,280 --> 00:34:22,389
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

786
00:34:17,969 --> 00:34:19,070
We'll know

787
00:34:19,070 --> 00:34:19,920
when they get back anyway.

788
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:21,110
Why bother calling?

789
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:24,610
[120]

790
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:25,610
[120; Emergency Rescue]

791
00:34:25,639 --> 00:34:26,889
[Fucheng Emergency Medical Rescue Center]

792
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,110
Her finger got crushed off by a machine.

793
00:34:29,110 --> 00:34:29,920
Did they bring the severed finger?

794
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:30,670
It's inside.

795
00:34:30,670 --> 00:34:31,150
Notify Orthopedics.

796
00:34:31,150 --> 00:34:31,840
Have them prepare immediately

797
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:32,880
for a finger replantation surgery.

798
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:33,230
Chen Junnan,

799
00:34:33,230 --> 00:34:34,070
you take the other patient.

800
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:34,360
Okay.

801
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:35,800
Make sure you thoroughly clean the wounds.

802
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:36,150
Give her

803
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,280
a thorough full-body examination.

804
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:37,670
Okay, okay.

805
00:34:37,670 --> 00:34:38,320
Let's go.

806
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:40,710
What's your problem?
Is this really necessary?

807
00:34:40,710 --> 00:34:41,800
These are the two patients

808
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:42,760
-I just told you about.
-Don't get worked up.

809
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:44,550
One has a severed left index finger.

810
00:34:44,550 --> 00:34:45,179
The severed finger

811
00:34:45,179 --> 00:34:46,760
is preserved in the transport container.

812
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:47,670
This patient has

813
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:48,920
a stab wound to the left forearm

814
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:50,320
and another to the thigh.

815
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:52,360
I'm not seriously hurt.

816
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,290
They're just superficial wounds.

817
00:34:54,510 --> 00:34:56,150
I gave you a checkup.

818
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,320
Of these two wounds,

819
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:01,920
this one here on your leg

820
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:03,760
is a little more serious.

821
00:35:04,110 --> 00:35:06,190
It's about 2.5 centimeters deep.

822
00:35:07,190 --> 00:35:08,710
But it hasn't hit any

823
00:35:08,710 --> 00:35:10,000
major blood vessels.

824
00:35:10,030 --> 00:35:11,710
I'll give it a quick treatment.

825
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:13,480
No wonder it doesn't hurt.

826
00:35:14,480 --> 00:35:15,710
All right. Take it down a notch.

827
00:35:15,710 --> 00:35:17,030
It'll hurt tonight.

828
00:35:19,070 --> 00:35:20,530
Why were you two fighting?

829
00:35:21,630 --> 00:35:23,440
We were both tricked by the same jerk.

830
00:35:23,440 --> 00:35:24,840
We're both victims here.

831
00:35:25,070 --> 00:35:27,190
Can you swear
you haven't been seeing Zang Tian?

832
00:35:27,190 --> 00:35:27,880
You homewrecker!

833
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:28,510
Who are you calling that?

834
00:35:28,510 --> 00:35:29,150
Come on.

835
00:35:29,320 --> 00:35:30,150
So what if I am?

836
00:35:30,150 --> 00:35:30,840
Homewrecker!

837
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:31,800
You tramp!

838
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:35,090
Stop fighting!

839
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:36,710
Then why were you two fighting?

840
00:35:36,710 --> 00:35:38,640
You should've gone after that guy!

841
00:35:39,550 --> 00:35:40,840
You're right.

842
00:35:42,550 --> 00:35:43,440
I'll find someone

843
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:44,840
to teach Zang Tian a lesson.

844
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,710
That's enough.

845
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:47,840
I'm not telling you
to go around hitting people.

846
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:49,920
You're young. You should obey the law.

847
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:50,800
I'm not that young.

848
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:51,920
I'm already 19.

849
00:35:53,710 --> 00:35:55,510
Look at my new hair color.

850
00:35:56,070 --> 00:35:57,000
Isn't it trendy?

851
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,280
Trendy

852
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:02,410
is about the most
outdated word you could use.

853
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:04,110
Doctor,

854
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:06,630
has anyone ever told you

855
00:36:06,670 --> 00:36:07,630
you're kind of handsome?

856
00:36:07,630 --> 00:36:08,400
That's enough.

857
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:09,760
I've treated both

858
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:10,670
of your wounds.

859
00:36:11,110 --> 00:36:12,670
If you feel any discomfort,

860
00:36:12,670 --> 00:36:13,670
let me know.

861
00:36:14,550 --> 00:36:15,760
But I noticed some blood

862
00:36:15,760 --> 00:36:16,510
on your underwear.

